        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A caller ordered $240 of pizza on {DATE} with a stolen card number and picked it up. The pizzeria's camera showed {D} at the counter. The pizzeria takes large orders by phone for pickup at the counter. The order was placed at about 5 p.m. and picked up an hour later, and the card owner disputed the charge two days afterward.",
