        role: "Party host",
        exam: [.direct("Tell us about your party and who was there.", "\"A backyard cookout for about thirty friends and neighbors. The grill was going, music was playing, and people were standing around in small groups.\""), .direct("What happened at your party?", "\"About thirty guests were in the backyard with a grill going. Around 9 p.m. there was an argument, and {D} sprayed pepper spray into the crowd.\""), .direct("Did you see {D} take the spray out?", "\"Yes, {D} pulled the spray from a bag and aimed it toward the group. I saw {D} aim.\""), .direct("What did {V} complain of?", "\"Burning eyes. {V} was coughing and could not see. Medics came at about 9:30 and treated {V}.\""), .direct("What led up to the spray?", "\"At about nine, {D} and another guest got into an argument near the grill. Voices were raised and a few of us stepped closer.\""), .direct("What exactly did {D} do?", "\"{D} reached into a bag, took out a small canister, and pointed it toward the group. There was a hiss and a cloud, and people started coughing.\""), .cross("Could it have gone off by accident?", "\"I saw {D} aim it. I do not think it was an accident, but it happened fast.\""), .cross("Was {D} arguing with someone before the spray?", "\"There was an argument at about 9. I did not hear all of it.\""), .cross("How far were you from {D}?", "\"About fifteen feet. I could see {D}'s arm raise, but the party was crowded.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} take the cap off the canister?", "\"I saw {D} holding it with the cap off, but I couldn't see when it came off.\""), .cross("How many people were affected?", "\"Six or seven people complained of burning eyes. {V} was the worst and needed medical care.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} sprayed people.", "An accident."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The cap was off.", "The bag was zipped."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you spray {V}?", "\"The spray went off. I did not mean to hit {V.him}. I was holding it, and it discharged.\""), .direct("Were you arguing with someone?", "\"A little. It was a heated moment, but nothing physical.\""), .direct("Did you aim at the crowd?", "\"No. I did not aim at anyone. I had it out because I was nervous.\""), .direct("Explain to the jury why you had pepper spray with you.", "\"I carry it for safety when I walk home late. It stays in my bag, and I'd put the bag on a chair by the grill.\""), .direct("What were you doing right before it went off?", "\"I was in a heated argument with another guest. I reached in my bag to get my keys, and my hand hit the canister.\""), .direct("What did you do when it sprayed?", "\"I dropped it and tried to help people rinse their eyes. I was horrified, and I called for water and for someone to call 911.\""), .cross("The cap was off the can, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. It was off because I had been holding it.\""), .cross("Why did you carry pepper spray to a backyard party?", "\"I carry it for my safety. I did not plan to use it.\""), .cross("Several guests say you aimed. Are they all wrong?", "\"They saw it from a distance. I did not aim.\""), .cross("The cap was off the canister. How did that happen?", "\"I'd been holding it earlier to check it, and I may have left the cap off. I didn't aim at anyone.\""), .cross("The host says you aimed it at the crowd. Is the host lying?", "\"The host saw part of it and drew a conclusion. I understand why, but I didn't aim.\"")],
        openings: ("During a backyard party with about thirty guests, {D} pulled pepper spray from a bag and sprayed it into the crowd after an argument. {V} was treated by medics for burning eyes.", "The defense case is that the spray discharged by accident during a heated moment and that {D} never meant to hit anyone."),
        closings: ("An argument at 9, spray into a crowd at 9:05, and medics at 9:30. The host saw {D} aim, and a crowd of guests was in the line of fire.", "{D} had a spray out, nervous in an argument, and it went off. The State must prove that {D} meant to spray {V}, and an accident is not an assault."),
        timeline: [(0, "9 p.m.: the argument."), (0, "9:05 p.m.: the spray."), (0, "9:30 p.m.: medics arrive.")],
