        role: "Landfill manager",
        exam: [.direct("Describe the landfill and how it is secured in your own words.", "\"It's a county landfill with a fence around the working area. The gate is locked after hours, and a camera records everyone who enters.\""), .direct("Was the landfill gate open that night?", "\"No. It was locked after hours, with a gate camera at the entrance. The landfill is fenced all around.\""), .direct("What did the gate camera show?", "\"{D} climbing the fence at about 10 p.m. Deputies arrived about half an hour later.\""), .direct("What notice had {D} been given?", "\"A written notice thirty days earlier telling {D} to stop scavenging at the landfill. It is in our file.\""), .direct("What had you done about {D} before that night?", "\"{D} had been caught scavenging twice. I sent a written notice thirty days earlier telling {D} to stop and that further entry would be treated as trespass.\""), .direct("What did the gate camera show on the night in question?", "\"At about ten at night, {D} approaches the fence, looks around, and climbs over near the gate. The camera records the whole climb.\""), .cross("Did {D} receive that notice personally?", "\"It was delivered in writing. I do not have a signed receipt, so I cannot swear {D} read it.\""), .cross("Was anything damaged at the landfill?", "\"No. The fence was not damaged. {D} climbed over, and I cannot say anything was taken.\""), .cross("Is the gate lock sometimes left open?", "\"The gate is locked after hours, but I cannot say what happened at 10 that night.\""), .cross("Did {D} acknowledge receiving the notice?", "\"I mailed it to the address on file. I don't have a signature, so I can't say {D} read it.\""), .cross("Was the gate locked that night?", "\"It was locked when we closed at five. I can't say whether anything happened to the lock afterward.\"")],
