        summary: "{D} tailgated a minivan for three miles on {DATE}, flashing lights, with a child inside the van. The two vehicles were on a main road with several lights and a school zone. The truck closed in at about 5 p.m., passed the minivan at 5:10 p.m., and the driver reported it at 5:20 p.m.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Dash Camera", "{D}'s truck within one car length."), E(.statement, 2, "Minivan Driver", "The truck stayed within one car length for three miles.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Slow Driver", "{DL} says the van was slow.")],
        role: "Minivan driver",
        exam: [.direct("Describe the drive and who was with you for the jury.", "\"I was driving my child home from after-school care on the main road at about five. It's a busy road with several lights and a school zone.\""), .direct("What did you see behind you on the road?", "\"A truck within about one car length of my minivan for three miles. The driver was flashing lights at me the whole way.\""), .direct("Who was in the van?", "\"My child and me. It was about 5 p.m. on a main road with several lights and a school zone.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I stayed at the speed limit and tried to stay calm. The truck passed me at about 5:10, and I reported it at 5:20.\""), .direct("How close was the truck behind you?", "\"About one car length the whole way, so close I couldn't see the headlights in my mirror. It flashed its high beams several times.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I stayed at the speed limit and kept my eyes on the road. I was scared and I didn't want to speed up with a child in the van.\""), .cross("Were you driving at the speed limit?", "\"Yes. I was at the limit the entire time. I was not speeding.\""), .cross("Might you have been driving slower than the traffic?", "\"I do not believe so. I drove at the limit, and the road had a school zone.\""), .cross("Did you brake suddenly or slow down on purpose?", "\"No. I stayed at the limit and didn't brake except for lights. I wasn't trying to block the truck.\""), .cross("Did the truck ever touch your van?", "\"No. It never touched the van, but it stayed that close for three miles.\""), .cross("Did the truck ever pass you in the school zone?", "\"Not in the school zone. The truck passed us afterward on a straight stretch, and I reported it to the sheriff about ten minutes later.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} drove recklessly.", "A slow driver."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The van was at the limit.", "{DL} passed the van afterward."),
        defendant: [.direct("Were you following close to the minivan?", "\"Yes, I was close. I was in a hurry and the van was moving slow.\""), .direct("Why were you so close?", "\"It was slow, and I wanted it to go faster. I did not think about how close I was.\""), .direct("Did you flash your lights?", "\"Yes. I flashed them to get the driver to move over. I did not mean to scare anyone.\""), .direct("Explain to the jury why you were in a hurry that afternoon.", "\"I was late to pick up a family member from work. I'd been stuck behind slow traffic on the main road.\""), .direct("Why did you flash your lights?", "\"To get the van to move over or speed up. I thought the driver was texting or distracted.\""), .direct("Did you know there was a child in the van?", "\"Not until I passed. I saw a car seat when I went by, and I felt terrible.\""), .cross("Three miles with a child in the van. Doesn't that scare a parent?", "\"I can see that it would. I did not know a child was there.\""), .cross("One car length is very close, isn't it?", "\"Yes, it is. I should have backed off.\""), .cross("You passed the van afterward, didn't you?", "\"I did. I wanted to get around it and go on my way.\""), .cross("Following that closely is dangerous. Didn't you realize that?", "\"I did, and I wasn't thinking. I was fixed on getting through the traffic.\""), .cross("The dash camera shows you within one car length for three miles. How do you explain that?", "\"I can't. I was angry and I was close, and I should have backed off.\"")],
        openings: ("A truck tailgated a minivan for three miles on a main road, within a car length, flashing its lights, with a child inside. {D} finally passed the van and the driver reported it.", "The defense witnesses will explain that {D} was in a hurry behind a slow vehicle and did not know a child was inside. It was impatience, not a threat."),
        closings: ("Three miles, a car length of space, flashing lights, and a child in the van. A truck that close to a minivan is not an accident.", "{D} was impatient, not malicious. {D} did not know a child was in the van and did not touch it. This was bad driving, and the law has a lesser name for it."),
