        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Man Tows Stolen Utility Trailer to Scrap Yard With Plates Removed"],
        law: "possStolen",
        spec: "Possessed a utility trailer valued at $1,900 belonging to {V}, knowing it to be stolen, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} towed a stolen utility trailer worth $1,900 to a scrap yard with the plates removed on {DATE}. The trailer was kept in a driveway with its tongue pointed to the street. It vanished overnight, {D} sold the frame the next day, and {V} found the listing that same day.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Scrap Slip", "{D} sold the trailer's frame."), E(.document, 2, "Registration", "The trailer is registered to {V}.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Bought", "{DL} says {D.he} bought it.")],
        role: "Trailer owner",
        exam: [.direct("Describe the trailer in your own words.", "\"A utility trailer I use for hauling lawn equipment. It was parked in my driveway with the tongue pointing toward the street.\""), .direct("Whose trailer was it?", "\"Mine. It is a utility trailer worth about $1,900, registered in my name. I kept it in my driveway with the tongue facing the street.\""), .direct("When did it disappear?", "\"Overnight. In the morning it was gone, and I found a listing for its frame the same day {D} sold it.\""), .direct("What had been done to it?", "\"The plates were removed. Later I learned the VIN had been ground off.\""), .direct("How did you find it after the theft?", "\"I saw a listing online of a trailer frame matching mine for sale at a scrap yard. The frame still had a faded stripe on it that I'd painted.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I called the yard, gave the registration number, and the yard confirmed that someone had sold them the frame. A deputy came and took the slip.\""), .cross("Whose name is on the registration?", "\"Mine. I have the registration, and it matches the trailer.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} take it?", "\"No. I did not see who took it. I learned about {D} from the scrap yard.\""), .cross("Is it common to keep a trailer in a driveway?", "\"Yes. Lots of people do, and I did not lock it.\""), .cross("Did the yard say who sold the frame?", "\"Yes, {D}. The slip shows {D}'s name and ID.\""), .cross("Did anyone see the trailer being taken from your driveway?", "\"No. It was gone in the morning and I didn't hear a thing.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} scrapped a stolen trailer.", "A purchase."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The VIN was ground off.", "No bill of sale exists."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you steal the trailer?", "\"No. I did not steal it. I bought the trailer from someone and sold the frame for scrap.\""), .direct("Did you sell the frame?", "\"Yes. I sold it to a scrap yard the next day. I got what the weight was worth.\""), .direct("Do you have a bill of sale?", "\"I lost it. I had a paper from the seller, and I cannot find it.\""), .direct("Tell the jury how you came to have the trailer.", "\"I bought it from a seller I met at a swap meet for $400. I didn't get a bill of sale, only a handshake.\""), .direct("Why did you sell the frame for scrap?", "\"The trailer was rusted and the bed was damaged. I needed money and the scrap yard paid about $120.\""), .direct("What did you notice about the VIN and the plates?", "\"The plates were already off when I got it, and I didn't see a VIN. I figured it was an old trailer from a farm.\""), .cross("The plates were removed, weren't they?", "\"They were off when I got it. I did not remove them.\""), .cross("You towed it to a scrap yard the same day a listing appeared?", "\"I did. I was trying to move it quickly, and I did not think about timing.\""), .cross("The VIN was ground off. Who did that?", "\"I don't know. It was that way when I got the trailer, and I didn't look closely.\""), .cross("You can't produce a bill of sale. Why should the jury believe you?", "\"I lost the slip the seller wrote. I understand how it looks, but I didn't steal anything.\""), .cross("You sold the frame for scrap the very next day, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I needed the money, and I believed the trailer was a junker I could dispose of. I did not think anyone would be looking for it.\"")],
        openings: ("A utility trailer worth $1,900 vanished overnight from the driveway of {V}'s home. The next day {D} sold the frame to a scrap yard, and a deputy traced it.", "Jurors will hear that {D} bought the trailer from someone else for $400 and sold it for scrap, believing it was a rusted old trailer with no owner to worry about."),
        closings: ("A stolen trailer, plates removed, VIN ground off, and {D} at the scrap yard the next day with the frame. No bill of sale exists.", "{D} bought a trailer and sold its frame, with a paper that was lost. The State has not shown that {D} took it from {V}'s driveway."),
