        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} looked back twice.", "{DL} had no headphones."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you pedal away from the deputy?", "\"I didn't hear the deputy tell me to stop. I was riding home and thought I was alone. I just kept riding.\""), .direct("Why did you go through yards?", "\"It's a shortcut I use to get home. I didn't know a deputy was behind me until I was in the alley.\""), .direct("What happened when you were caught?", "\"I stopped and told the deputy I hadn't heard anything. I wasn't trying to run. I was surprised and out of breath.\""), .direct("Tell the jury what you were doing on the bike that night.", "\"I was riding home from a friend's house. It's about two miles, and I take shortcuts through yards and alleys.\""), .direct("Why was there no front light?", "\"The battery had died the week before and I hadn't replaced it. I rode that route in the dark all the time.\""), .direct("What did you notice about the patrol car?", "\"I saw lights behind me at the end of the street. I thought it was a car turning, so I kept going.\""), .cross("The body camera shows the deputy giving an order, doesn't it?", "\"It does. I didn't hear it at the time. The camera has better ears than I do.\""), .cross("You rode through yards for ten minutes, didn't you?", "\"I was trying to get home. I wasn't thinking about the deputy. I didn't know there was a chase.\""), .cross("You had no light on your bike, did you?", "\"No. I know I own that. That's a mistake, and I'm sorry for it.\""), .cross("The deputy called out. Why didn't you stop?", "\"I didn't hear it. I was listening to music on a small speaker clipped to my bag.\""), .cross("You looked back twice, according to the video. Doesn't that mean you knew?", "\"I looked because of the lights. I didn't realize it was for me.\"")],
