        spec: "Stole a rented trailer valued at $900 belonging to {V}, a rental company, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} kept a rented trailer for three weeks past the contract date on {DATE} and ignored calls. The rental company hires out utility trailers by the day and keeps a contract on file. The trailer was due back twenty-one days before the company reported it, and it was found two days later at {D}'s.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Rental Contract", "The trailer was due back three weeks earlier."), E(.statement, 2, "Rental Manager", "Called {D} several times about the trailer.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Extension", "{DL} says {D.he} asked for more time.")],
        role: "Rental manager",
        exam: [.direct("Describe your rental company and how trailers are rented for the jury.", "\"We rent utility trailers by the day or week. The renter signs a contract with a return date and a daily late fee, and we keep a copy on file.\""), .direct("When was the trailer due back?", "\"The contract set a due date three weeks earlier. The trailer was twenty-one days overdue when we reported it.\""), .direct("What did you do about it?", "\"I called {D} several times. The calls went unanswered, and I left messages.\""), .direct("What happened to the trailer?", "\"It was found two days after we reported it, at {D}'s place. No extension is on file.\""), .direct("What did the contract say about the due date?", "\"It set a return date three weeks before we reported the trailer overdue, with a daily fee of $25 after that. The contract is signed and initialed by {D}.\""), .direct("How did you find the trailer?", "\"Two days after we reported it to deputies, a deputy located it in the driveway at {D}'s home. It was hitched to a pickup and had a load of lumber.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever ask for an extension?", "\"Not that I recorded. There is none in our file, but I cannot rule out a conversation.\""), .cross("Did {D} refuse to return it?", "\"I never spoke to {D}, so I cannot say. I only know the calls went unanswered.\""), .cross("Was the trailer damaged?", "\"No. It was returned in usable condition. {D} had been using it for jobs.\""), .cross("Did you speak with {D} at any point?", "\"Once, early on, and {D} said the trailer would come back soon. After that the calls went to voicemail.\""), .cross("Is there any record of an extension?", "\"No. {D} may have asked in a call I missed, but nothing is in our system.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} kept a trailer.", "A late return."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("No extension is on file.", "{DL} used it for hauling jobs."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you keep the trailer past the due date?", "\"Yes. I kept it for extra time, because I had hauling jobs that ran longer than I planned.\""), .direct("Did you get calls from the rental company?", "\"I missed them. My phone was off a lot while I was working, and I did not check the messages.\""), .direct("Did you intend to keep the trailer?", "\"No. I planned to bring it back as soon as the jobs were done.\""), .direct("Please describe your trailer rental.", "\"I rented a trailer to haul material for a remodeling job. I signed for three days and planned to return it the same week.\""), .direct("What happened with the job?", "\"It ran long because of rain and delays, and I kept the trailer to finish. I thought I could return it as soon as the job was done.\""), .direct("Why didn't you answer the calls?", "\"My phone was cracked and I missed most of them. I'd get a voicemail and mean to call back, and then another job would start.\""), .cross("Three weeks is a long time to miss calls, isn't it?", "\"It is. I was busy, and I should have called back.\""), .cross("No extension was on file, was there?", "\"I thought we had an agreement for more time. I should have made sure it was in writing.\""), .cross("You used the trailer for paid jobs, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I was making money with it, and I should have kept the rental current.\""), .cross("Three weeks is a long time. Didn't you realize you owed fees?", "\"I knew I'd owe something. I planned to pay it all when I returned the trailer.\""), .cross("You used the trailer for other jobs. Isn't that keeping it for yourself?", "\"I used it for the remodeling job I rented it for. I should have returned it first.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} rented a utility trailer and kept it three weeks past the contract date, ignoring several calls from the rental company. The trailer was found two days after it was reported, at {D}'s place.", "By the end of this trial, the proof will show that {D} meant to return the trailer after a run of hauling jobs and simply missed the calls. {D} never meant to keep it."),
        closings: ("A contract with a due date, three weeks of silence, and a trailer found at {D}'s place. No extension was asked for, and no call was returned.", "{D} kept a trailer a little too long during a busy stretch. That is a rental problem, and the State has not proved {D} intended to keep it."),
        timeline: [(-21, "The trailer is due."), (0, "The company reports it."), (2, "It is found at {D}'s.")],
        identified: "Rental Contract",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let campgroundHookups = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.campgroundHookups",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Camper Hooks Up to County Electric Box for Weeks Without Paying"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole electricity valued at $240 belonging to {V}, a county campground, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} ran a cord to a campground electric box for six weeks on {DATE} without paying. The county campground has numbered sites with electric boxes and a posted nightly rate. {D} arrived six weeks earlier, and the ranger read the meter and wrote the report the same day.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Meter Log", "The box showed unpaid use."), E(.document, 2, "Camper Rules", "The posted nightly rate and rules.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Included", "{DL} says power was included.")],
        role: "Ranger",
        exam: [.direct("Tell us about the campground and how sites are assigned.", "\"It's a county campground with forty numbered sites. Some have electric hookups, and a posted rate of $9 a night covers a site without power and $19 with it.\""), .direct("What did you find at the campground on {DATE}?", "\"A cord running from a numbered site to an electric box. The meter showed unpaid use over about six weeks.\""), .direct("How long had {DL} been there?", "\"{D} arrived six weeks earlier. I read the meter and wrote my report that same day, so the dates are solid.\""), .direct("What are the campground rules?", "\"There's a posted nightly rate and written rules for campers. Electric use is part of the fee, and it's posted at the site.\""), .direct("What did you find at {D}'s site?", "\"A long orange cord running from the electric box on the next site to {D}'s camper. The box wasn't assigned to {D}, and the meter showed six weeks of use.\""), .direct("How did you determine it was unpaid?", "\"I checked the reservation system and found {D} was registered for a no-power site. The electric box was on a different site that had no reservation.\""), .cross("{DL} says power was included, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"At this campground, power is part of a paid site, but {D} hadn't paid. That's the point.\""), .cross("Did {DL} try to hide the cord?", "\"No. It was in plain view, plugged into the box at the site. {D} didn't try to conceal it.\""), .cross("Did you ever talk to {DL} before that day?", "\"Not about this. I'd seen {D} around, but I hadn't discussed payment. I only found it on my meter check.\""), .cross("Did {D} sign the camper rules?", "\"Yes, at check-in. The rules say hookups are only for sites that pay the electric rate.\""), .cross("What did {D} say about the nightly rate when you spoke with {D}?", "\"{D} said {D} thought power was included in the site. The posted rate was $9 a night, and {D} had signed the camper rules.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took power.", "An included hookup."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The posted rate was $9 a night.", "{DL} signed the rules."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you plug into the campground box?", "\"I thought power was included with the site. I didn't see any sign saying otherwise. I'd been camping there for weeks.\""), .direct("Did you pay for the site?", "\"I thought I had paid what I was supposed to. I never knew there was a separate charge for power. No one told me.\""), .direct("Did you try to hide the cord?", "\"No. It was in plain view. I wouldn't do that if I thought I was doing something wrong.\""), .direct("Tell the jury how long you've camped and why.", "\"I've been living in the camper for about two months while I look for work. I pay for a site by the week.\""), .direct("Why did you run a cord to that box?", "\"The site had an electric box and I thought power came with the rate. Nobody told me otherwise at check-in.\""), .direct("What did you do when the ranger told you?", "\"I apologized and unplugged the cord. I offered to pay for the power I'd used.\""), .cross("The rate and rules were posted, weren't they?", "\"Probably. I didn't read them closely. I should have. I just assumed power came with a site.\""), .cross("You stayed six weeks without paying, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I didn't realize I hadn't paid enough. I'm willing to pay what I owe.\""), .cross("The meter showed use the whole time, didn't it?", "\"I'm sure it did. I used the power for ordinary things like lights and cooking. I wasn't running anything unusual.\""), .cross("The rules sheet says hookups cost extra. Didn't you read it?", "\"I read the part about quiet hours. I didn't read every line, and In hindsight, yes.\""), .cross("Six weeks is a long time to not notice you hadn't paid for power.", "\"I assumed it was part of my site fee. I wasn't trying to get anything for free.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} ran a cord to a campground electric box and used it for six weeks without paying. The ranger read the meter and wrote the report the same day. The State will show the meter log and the posted rules.", "The defense will point you to a camper who believed power was included, ran the cord in plain view, and never tried to avoid the rules."),
        closings: ("Six weeks, an electric box, and a meter showing unpaid use. The rates and the rules were posted, and {D} chose to plug in and not pay.", "{D} plugged in openly and believed power came with the site. The State has not proved {D} meant to steal electricity rather than made an honest mistake."),
        timeline: [(-42, "{DL} arrives."), (0, "The ranger reads the meter."), (0, "The ranger writes a report.")],
        identified: "Meter Log",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let hayBaleTheft = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.hayBaleTheft",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Hay Bales Taken From Field by Man With Flatbed"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole hay bales valued at $480 belonging to {V}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Forty hay bales were taken from a field overnight on {DATE}. A neighbor saw {D}'s flatbed. The bales were stacked at the edge of the field and tied with the owner's twine. The owner counted them the next morning, and the neighbor shared the sighting of the flatbed that day.",
        state: [E(.statement, 3, "Neighbor", "{D}'s flatbed at the field."), E(.document, 2, "Bale Count", "Forty bales missing from the field after the owner's count.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Sold", "{DL} says a man sold them to {D.him}.")],
        role: "Farm owner",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell us about your farm and how you store hay.", "\"I have a cattle farm and bale hay each summer. I stack the bales at the edge of the field and tie each one with blue twine that I buy by the roll.\""), .direct("What did you lose on {DATE}?", "\"Forty hay bales were taken from my field overnight. They were stacked at the edge of the field and tied with my twine.\""), .direct("How do you know how many were missing?", "\"I counted them the next morning. Forty were gone from the stack. I count them often because hay is money to me.\""), .direct("How did you discover the bales were gone?", "\"I walked the field the next morning and the stack was nearly empty. I counted and forty bales were gone, and I saw tire tracks leading to the road.\""), .direct("What did your neighbor see?", "\"A flatbed truck parked at the field entrance at about eleven that night. The neighbor recognized the truck as {D}'s and told me the next day.\""), .direct("How did you recognize that the bales at {D}'s place were yours?", "\"My twine was still on them. I tie every bale with the same cord and a knot I use, so I knew them at once.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} take the bales?", "\"No. I was asleep. I counted in the morning, and I'm relying on my neighbor for the flatbed.\""), .cross("Couldn't another flatbed have been at the field?", "\"I suppose so. The neighbor says it was {D}'s. I can't say that for myself.\""), .cross("Can you prove the bales {DL} has are yours?", "\"I recognize my twine, but twine is twine. I can't prove from a photo whose bales they are.\""), .cross("Did anyone see {D} load the bales?", "\"No. The neighbor saw the truck, not anyone loading hay.\""), .cross("Are there other flatbeds in the area?", "\"Plenty. Farm trucks are common here, and I can't say whose truck it was for certain.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took hay.", "A purchase."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("My twine was on the bales.", "No receipt."),
        defendant: [.direct("Where did you get the hay?", "\"A seller I met sold it to me. I paid cash, and the seller said there was extra hay to sell. I loaded it on my flatbed.\""), .direct("Were you at {V}'s field?", "\"No. I've never been on that farm. I drove my flatbed to pick up hay from the seller, and that was somewhere else.\""), .direct("Did you know it was stolen?", "\"No. If I'd known, I wouldn't have bought it. I thought I was buying from a farmer who had extra.\""), .direct("Tell the jury about the hay you bought.", "\"I bought forty bales from a seller at the side of a rural road. I paid cash and loaded them onto my flatbed.\""), .direct("Why did you buy hay that way?", "\"The price was good and I needed hay for my animals. I didn't think about where it came from.\""), .direct("Were you ever at {V}'s farm?", "\"Never. I've driven that road, but I've never been on the property.\""), .cross("You can't give a name for the seller, can you?", "\"No. I didn't ask for a card or a receipt. I know I should have.\""), .cross("Forty bales is a lot of hay, isn't it?", "\"It is. I'd planned to use it for my own animals. I didn't think anything about the quantity.\""), .cross("Your flatbed was seen at the field, wasn't it?", "\"That's what the neighbor says. I wasn't there. A lot of flatbeds look alike.\""), .cross("The bales had {V}'s twine on them. Didn't you notice?", "\"Blue twine is common. I didn't look at the twine.\""), .cross("You can't name the seller. Why not?", "\"It was a quick cash deal and I didn't get a card or a name. I wish I'd asked.\"")],
        openings: ("Forty hay bales, tied with {V}'s twine, were taken from a field overnight. A neighbor saw {D}'s flatbed there, and the owner counted forty missing in the morning. The State will present the farm owner and the neighbor.", "The defense will present a buyer who paid cash for hay from a seller, never set foot on {V}'s farm, and is accused because a neighbor thought a flatbed looked familiar."),
        closings: ("Forty bales gone from a stack overnight, a flatbed seen at the field, and {D}'s truck matches it. The simplest answer is the one the neighbor gave.", "A flatbed in the dark and a neighbor's guess. The State cannot show {D} was at the field or that the hay {D} has came from there."),
        timeline: [(0, "Night: the field."), (1, "The owner counts bales."), (1, "A neighbor shares the flatbed.")],
        identified: "Neighbor",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let catchBasinCover = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.catchBasinCover",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Metal Storm Drain Covers Lifted and Sold to Scrap Yard"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole storm drain covers valued at $750 belonging to {V}, a town, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Six storm drain covers were pulled up and sold to a scrap yard on {DATE}. The yard slip bears {D}'s ID. The openings were left uncovered in the street, and the town traced the covers to the scrap yard two days after they vanished.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Scrap Slip", "{D}'s ID on a slip for six covers."), E(.document, 2, "Town Inventory", "Six covers on the town's replacement list.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Found", "{DL} says {D.he} found them.")],
        role: "Town public works",
        exam: [.direct("Tell us about the town's storm drains and how covers are maintained.", "\"The town maintains about four hundred catch basins. Covers are cast iron stamped with the town's name, and we keep a replacement list.\""), .direct("What did you find on {DATE}?", "\"Six storm drain covers were pulled up, leaving open holes in the street. It was a hazard to every car and pedestrian on the road.\""), .direct("How did you trace them?", "\"Two days later, we traced them to a scrap yard. The yard's slip bears {D}'s ID for six covers sold.\""), .direct("How do you know they were the town's?", "\"They're on our replacement list. We had six covers listed, and the count matches what the scrap yard bought.\""), .direct("What did you find that morning?", "\"Six open holes in the street where covers had been pulled up. Traffic cones had been put out by a resident, and a car had already hit one of the openings.\""), .direct("How did you trace the covers?", "\"A scrap yard called after a seller brought in iron stamped with the town's name. The slip had {D}'s ID on it.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} pull the covers?", "\"No. I only know what the scrap slip shows. I wasn't there when they were taken.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} found them, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"I find that hard to believe for six covers. They're heavy and set in the street.\""), .cross("Did anyone get hurt by the open drains?", "\"Not that I know of. We put out cones and replaced them quickly, but it was dangerous for a couple of days.\""), .cross("How heavy is a cover, and how would someone lift one?", "\"Seventy to eighty pounds each. A person needs a pry bar and a vehicle to move six of them.\""), .cross("The town never put up a warning near the open drains, did it?", "\"We put out cones the same day we found them. I do not know how long they were open before then, because we only learned from a resident.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} sold town property.", "Found scrap."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The town stamp is on the covers.", "No hauling permit."),
        defendant: [.direct("How did you come to sell the covers?", "\"I found them. They were lying near the road, and it looked like they'd been left. I took them to the scrap yard.\""), .direct("Did you pull them from the street?", "\"No. I never pulled anything up. I found them already lifted, and I thought they were junk.\""), .direct("Why did you use your own ID at the yard?", "\"Because I wasn't hiding anything. I thought I was selling scrap I'd found, and the yard asks for ID.\""), .direct("Walk us through how you came across the covers.", "\"I was driving on a back road and saw several of them lying in a ditch. They looked like abandoned scrap.\""), .direct("What did you do with them?", "\"I loaded them into my truck and took them to the scrap yard. I used my ID because I had nothing to hide.\""), .direct("Did you think about whether they belonged to anyone?", "\"I assumed they'd been dumped. I didn't notice the town's stamp until later.\""), .cross("Six covers is a lot to just find, isn't it?", "\"It sounds bad, I know. They were in a pile. I didn't think about whether they belonged to anyone.\""), .cross("Storm drain covers belong to the town, don't they?", "\"Yes. I should have thought of that. I took the money and didn't ask questions.\""), .cross("The slip has your ID on it, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. I sold them. I'm not denying that. I'm saying I didn't know they were stolen.\""), .cross("Six covers is a lot to just find. Where exactly were they?", "\"In a ditch on a back road, about two miles from town. I can show you the spot.\""), .cross("The stamp on the covers says the town's name. Didn't you see it?", "\"I saw writing, but I didn't read it closely. I wish I had.\"")],
        openings: ("Six storm drain covers were pulled up and sold to a scrap yard, leaving open holes in the street. The yard's slip carries {D}'s ID, and the covers are on the town's replacement list. The State will show the slip and the inventory.", "Jurors will also see a scrap seller who used a real ID, claims the covers were already lifted when found, and never touched them in the street."),
        closings: ("Six covers pulled, six covers sold, and a scrap yard slip that carries {D}'s ID. Open holes were left in the street, and the evidence points to the person who sold them.", "{D} sold scrap in plain view and believed it was abandoned. The State has not proved {D} pulled the covers or knew they were stolen."),
        timeline: [(0, "Night: the covers vanish."), (1, "{D} sells them."), (2, "The town traces them.")],
        identified: "Scrap Slip",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let streetSignTheft = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.streetSignTheft",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Street Signs Removed From Road, Found in Dorm Room"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole street signs valued at $320 belonging to {V}, a county, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Four street signs were removed from a rural road on {DATE} and found in {D}'s dorm room. The signs, worth $320 together, came down from poles along the rural road overnight. The county received a tip two days later, and the room was searched the next day.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Signs", "Four signs in {D}'s room.", .search), E(.document, 2, "County Work Order", "Four signs reported missing from the rural road.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Gift", "{DL} says a friend gave them.")],
        role: "Public works supervisor",
        exam: [.direct("Describe the signs and how they're maintained for the jury.", "\"The county maintains the road signs on rural roads. Each sign is bolted to a pole with two bolts, and we log each sign on a work order.\""), .direct("What was missing from the rural road?", "\"Four street signs, worth about $320 together. They were removed from poles along the road overnight.\""), .direct("How did you learn where they were?", "\"The county received a tip two days later, and the room was searched the next day. All four signs were in {D}'s dorm room.\""), .direct("How do you know they are ours?", "\"The county work order lists the four signs, and the bolts matched the poles they came off of.\""), .direct("What did you find when you went out?", "\"Four signs were gone from poles along a three-mile stretch. The bolts had been unscrewed, and no damage was done to the poles.\""), .direct("What did you do once you were told the signs were in a dorm room?", "\"I went with deputies, matched the bolts and the sign numbers to our work order, and recovered all four signs. I also checked the poles to see which bolts were missing.\""), .cross("Could someone else have put them in the dorm room?", "\"I suppose so, but they were in {D}'s room. I cannot say who carried them.\""), .cross("Did {D} cooperate with the search?", "\"Yes. {D} was cooperative and told the officers it was a gift.\""), .cross("Did anyone see {D} take the signs?", "\"No. We have no witness who saw the signs being removed.\""), .cross("Are your signs distinctive or marked in any way?", "\"They carry the county's stamp on the back. The ones in {D}'s room matched our work order.\""), .cross("The signs could have been taken by someone else and left in {D}'s room, couldn't they?", "\"That is possible. I cannot say who removed them from the poles, only that they were in the room and the bolts matched our poles.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took signs.", "A gift."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The bolts matched the poles.", "The friend left."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take the street signs?", "\"No. They were a gift. A friend gave them to me and I did not think anything of it.\""), .direct("Who gave them to you?", "\"A friend I know as Skip. Skip left, and I do not know where.\""), .direct("Were you going to keep them?", "\"They were a gift, so I hung them on the wall as decoration. I did not know they were taken from poles.\""), .direct("Describe your dorm room and the signs for the jury.", "\"I'm a student and I share a room. I hung the signs on the wall as decoration, and my roommate liked them.\""), .direct("Where did you get them?", "\"A friend I know as Skip gave them to me as a joke. Skip left school a few weeks later, and I don't have a number.\""), .direct("Did you know they were county property?", "\"I thought they were souvenirs. Skip said they were old signs from a yard sale.\""), .cross("Street signs do not come as gifts, do they?", "\"I realize how that sounds. I thought they were novelty signs, and I did not ask.\""), .cross("The bolts matched the county's poles, didn't they?", "\"I did not notice. I did not look at the signs that closely.\""), .cross("Can you find this friend?", "\"No. Skip is gone. I know that makes this hard for me.\""), .cross("Street signs don't come as gifts. Didn't that seem strange?", "\"It did, a little. I figured Skip had gotten them somewhere legitimate.\""), .cross("The bolts matched the poles. How do you explain that?", "\"I don't. I didn't take them, and I didn't know where they came from.\"")],
        openings: ("Four street signs worth $320 disappeared from poles along a rural road overnight. Two days after a tip to the county, all four were found hanging in {D}'s dorm room.", "The defense case is that a friend gave {D} the signs as a gift and that {D} never went near those poles. The signs were a decoration, not a trophy."),
        closings: ("Four county signs, bolts that match the poles, and all four in {D}'s dorm room. A person with stolen property in hand has to explain it, and the explanation has run away.", "A gift from a friend who left, and no witness who saw {D} at any pole. The State must prove {D} knew the signs were stolen, and it has not."),
        timeline: [(0, "Night: the signs vanish."), (2, "A tip."), (3, "The room is searched.")],
        identified: "Signs",
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["searchSeizure"])

    static let houseSitter = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.houseSitter",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["House Sitter Wears Owner's Jewelry and Sells a Watch"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole a watch valued at $750 belonging to {V}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D}, a house sitter, sold {V}'s watch for $120 on {DATE} and wore a necklace in a photo. {V} had left the house in {D}'s care a week earlier. The watch was worth $750, and {V} saw the photo of the necklace a week after the sale.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Photo", "{D} wears {V}'s necklace."), E(.document, 2, "Watch Appraisal", "The watch is worth $750.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Permission", "{DL} says {V} allowed it.")],
        role: "Homeowner",
        exam: [.direct("What can you tell us about your trip and why you hired {D}?", "\"I was going out of town for a week and needed someone to watch the house and feed the cat. {D} was recommended by a friend.\""), .direct("What did you leave in {DL}'s care?", "\"My house for a week. {D} was the house sitter. I left a $750 watch there and a necklace in the house.\""), .direct("What happened to the watch?", "\"{D} sold it for $120. A pawn ticket shows it. I never gave anyone permission to sell it.\""), .direct("How did you learn about the necklace?", "\"A week after the sale, I saw a photo where {D} was wearing my necklace. That's when I knew something was wrong.\""), .direct("What did you tell {D} before you left?", "\"To feed the cat, water the plants, and bring in the mail. I said nothing about touching my jewelry, and I locked my bedroom closet.\""), .direct("How did you find out about the watch and the necklace?", "\"A week after I got back, a friend sent me a photo from social media. It showed {D} wearing my necklace. A pawn shop later confirmed {D} sold my watch.\""), .cross("{DL} says you allowed it, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"I never said anything of the kind. I'd never let a house sitter sell a watch.\""), .cross("Is there anything in writing about the watch?", "\"No. I never wrote anything down. I trusted {D}, and I'd never expect to need to write it.\""), .cross("Did you know {DL} well?", "\"Reasonably. I'd used {D} before for small jobs. That's why I trusted {D} with the house.\""), .cross("Did you give {D} a key to the closet?", "\"No. The closet was locked, but a key was in a drawer in the bedroom. I don't know how {D} got in.\""), .cross("Did you text {D} about using any of your things?", "\"No. I'd never given permission, and I would remember it.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took jewelry.", "Permission."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("A pawn ticket bears {D}'s ID.", "No text of permission."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you wear the necklace?", "\"It was in the house, and {V} told me to help myself to a few things. I wore it for a photo. I thought it was fine.\""), .direct("Did you mean to steal from {V}?", "\"No. I would never do that. I thought I had permission, and I never hid what I did.\""), .direct("Tell us how you came to wear the necklace.", "\"It was on the dresser, and {V} had said to treat the house like my own. I wore it for a photo and put it back.\""), .direct("Why did you sell the watch?", "\"{V} mentioned to me earlier that the watch wasn't working and was going to be thrown out. I sold it for $120 to a pawn shop.\""), .direct("What did you do when {V} called you?", "\"I told {V} what I'd done and offered to buy the watch back. {V} was angry and went to deputies.\""), .direct("What did you do in the house during the week you watched it?", "\"I fed the plants, brought in the mail, and kept the doors locked. I also looked through drawers I should have left alone, and I am not proud of that.\""), .cross("You sold a $750 watch for $120, didn't you?", "\"Yes. That's what I got. I took what the shop offered, and I thought {V} knew.\""), .cross("{V} says that no permission was given, doesn't {V.he}?", "\"That's what {V} says. I believe I was told it was fine. We may have misunderstood each other.\""), .cross("You posted a photo wearing the necklace, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I wasn't hiding. If I'd known it was wrong, I wouldn't have put it online.\""), .cross("A $750 watch for $120. Doesn't that tell you it wasn't yours to sell?", "\"I understand now. I believed it was broken, and I took what I could get.\""), .cross("You had no text from {V} saying you could sell it. Why not?", "\"I took a casual remark as permission. I should have asked.\"")],
