        summary: "Cash disappeared from a kitchen drawer over several visits by {D}, a babysitter, totaling $320 by {DATE}. The cash was kept in a kitchen drawer within {D}'s reach during visits, and the first visit was three weeks before the camera recorded a taking. {V} reported it the next day.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Kitchen Camera", "{D} takes bills from the drawer."), E(.document, 2, "Drawer Counts", "{V}'s notes of cash missing across several visits.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Pay", "{DL} says it was owed pay.")],
        role: "Parent",
        exam: [.direct("Tell the jury about {D}'s role in your home.", "\"{D} was our babysitter for about six months, watching our two children two or three evenings a week.\""), .direct("What does the kitchen camera show?", "\"{D} taking bills from the drawer. It shows five takings in all, though the first visit with missing cash was three weeks before the camera.\""), .direct("Did you owe {D} anything?", "\"No. We paid weekly, and pay was up to date. I owed {D} nothing.\""), .direct("How did you notice cash missing?", "\"We kept an envelope of cash in a kitchen drawer for the household. Over a few weeks the total kept coming up short, by $20 or $40 at a time.\""), .direct("How did you work out how much was missing from the drawer?", "\"I kept a small note of what I put in each week. When the count was $20 or $40 short on several visits, I knew it was not a miscount.\""), .direct("What did you do after you saw the camera footage?", "\"I called {D} and then the sheriff's office. I kept the footage and my notes so deputies could compare the visits and the amounts.\""), .cross("{D} says you owed {D.him} money, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"That is what {D} says. I paid every week, and I can show it.\""), .cross("Was the drawer within {D}'s reach during visits?", "\"Yes, the drawer is in the kitchen, where the babysitter is. That is why I started counting.\""), .cross("Did you ever tell {D} about the missing cash before the camera?", "\"No. I wanted to be sure first.\""), .cross("Were you late paying {D} at any point?", "\"No. We paid weekly and always on time. I checked the payments before talking to deputies.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever mention being owed extra hours?", "\"Not to me. If there had been a dispute over pay, I would have settled it.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took cash.", "Owed pay."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The camera shows five takings.", "Pay was up to date."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take money from the drawer?", "\"I took some. I believed I was owed it for extra hours I had worked.\""), .direct("How did you keep track of what you were owed?", "\"Roughly, in my head. I did not write it down, and I know that is a weakness.\""), .direct("Did you tell {V} you took it?", "\"No. I should have talked to {V.him} first. I was embarrassed to ask about money.\""), .direct("Please tell us about your work for the family.", "\"I watched the children after school and some evenings. I did extra hours sometimes when a parent worked late.\""), .direct("Why did you take the cash?", "\"I thought I was owed for extra hours that weren't paid. I took a little at a time and told myself it was fair.\""), .direct("Did you tell the family you were taking money?", "\"No. I should have talked to {V} first. I was afraid to bring it up.\""), .cross("The camera shows five takings. Were all of them for hours owed?", "\"I thought so. I cannot say each time exactly.\""), .cross("{V} says pay was up to date. Why didn't you believe that?", "\"I counted extra hours that I thought were not paid. I may have been wrong.\""), .cross("You took cash from a drawer in someone's kitchen without asking, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I should have asked. It was not the right way to handle it.\""), .cross("Five takings over three weeks. Weren't you stealing?", "\"I see how it looks. I believed I was owed, and I didn't think of it as stealing at the time.\""), .cross("You kept no record of the extra hours. How can anyone know what you were owed?", "\"I kept track in my head. I know now that's not good enough.\"")],
