        state: [E(.document, 3, "Bank Records", "Team money paid {D}'s phone and utilities."), E(.document, 2, "Fee Ledger", "Fees collected from team families.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Loan", "{DL} says {D.he} meant to repay.")],
        role: "Team president",
        exam: [.direct("What can you tell us about the swim team and how fees are handled?", "\"It's a youth swim team with about sixty swimmers. Families pay registration fees of about $200 each, and the treasurer deposits them into the team's checking account.\""), .direct("What did you find when you reviewed the swim team's account?", "\"The balance was short. The fees came in from team families sixty days before I reviewed it, and some of the money had been spent.\""), .direct("What did the bank records show?", "\"$1,600 of team money went to {D}'s phone and utilities. {D} was the treasurer, so the account was in {D}'s hands.\""), .direct("What did the fee ledger show?", "\"Fees collected from the team families. It lists what came in, and the total was far above what the account held.\""), .direct("How did you discover the shortage?", "\"I asked for a bank statement before the season-end banquet. The balance was about $1,600 lower than the fee ledger showed.\""), .direct("Where did the money go?", "\"The statements show payments to a phone company and a utility, in {D}'s name. They were made by debit card over about two months.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} meant to repay, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"I don't doubt {D} wanted to. But the team didn't authorize any loan.\""), .cross("Did {DL} hide the withdrawals?", "\"Not that I know of. They were in the bank records for anyone to see. I just hadn't looked until sixty days later.\""), .cross("Did {DL} do good work as treasurer?", "\"In general, yes. {D} was reliable, and that's why no one checked sooner. It's part of why this hurts.\""), .cross("Did you approve any loan to {D}?", "\"No. The board never discussed a loan, and nobody would have approved one.\""), .cross("Have you gotten any of the money back?", "\"{D} made one payment of $100 after we confronted {D.him}. Nothing since.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} used team money.", "A loan."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("No loan was approved.", "Receipts were missing."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you use team money?", "\"I was in a bad spot financially. I used the money for my phone and utilities, and I planned to put it back.\""), .direct("Did you plan to repay it?", "\"Yes. Every bit of it. I thought I could replace it before anyone looked. That was a mistake.\""), .direct("Did you tell anyone?", "\"No. I was ashamed. I should have asked the president for help instead of using the account.\""), .direct("Tell us about your job as treasurer.", "\"I volunteered because my child swims. I collected checks, made deposits, and paid for pool rental and awards.\""), .direct("What happened in your own life that season?", "\"I lost hours at work and fell behind on rent and bills. I used the team's debit card to pay my phone and utilities.\""), .direct("What did you plan to do?", "\"Repay it when my hours came back. I told myself it was a short-term loan.\""), .cross("$1,600 of team fees went to your bills, didn't it?", "\"Yes. I know it sounds bad. I treated the account like a loan, and I shouldn't have.\""), .cross("No one approved a loan, did they?", "\"No. I never asked. I didn't think they'd say yes, so I didn't ask.\""), .cross("The families trusted you with their fees, didn't they?", "\"Yes, and I let them down. I'm so sorry. I'll pay it all back.\""), .cross("You never told anyone you were using the team's money. Why?", "\"I was ashamed. I should have asked for help, and I know that asking the board was the right thing.\""), .cross("$1,600 over two months isn't a short loan. Isn't that taking?", "\"It started small and grew. I see now that I crossed a line.\"")],
        openings: ("{D}, the swim team treasurer, spent $1,600 of team fees on a phone and utilities. When the team president reviewed the account sixty days after the fees came in, the balance was short. The State will show the bank records and the ledger.", "Jurors will also see a treasurer who fell on hard times, planned to repay every dollar, and was never hiding anything. {D} borrowed money, and no one lost a cent."),
