        role: "Sheriff's deputy",
        exam: [.direct("Tell the jury how the call came in.", "\"At about two in the morning, a neighbor called about a loud generator. Dispatch sent me to a residential street at 3 a.m.\""), .direct("Why were you called?", "\"Neighbors called twice about the noise before I arrived. The generator had started at 11 p.m.\""), .direct("Was there still a power outage?", "\"No. Power had returned at midnight, three hours before I got there.\""), .direct("What did you hear when you arrived?", "\"A gas generator running in a driveway, loud enough that I could hear it with my windows up. The lights were on in the house.\""), .direct("What did {D} say?", "\"{D} said the power had been out during the storm and that {D.he} had started the generator to run the freezer. {D} didn't realize the power had come back.\""), .direct("What did you find when you walked to the back of {D}'s house?", "\"A large generator running on a pad near the neighbors' fence. Lights were on up and down the street, so I knew power had come back.\""), .cross("The storm caused an outage, didn't it?", "\"Yes. There had been an outage, and the generator made sense at first.\""), .cross("Did {D} refuse to turn it off?", "\"No. When I spoke to {D}, it was shut off. {D} was surprised.\""), .cross("Did you speak to the neighbors who called?", "\"Yes. They said they had been trying to sleep and called twice.\""), .cross("Did you check the grid?", "\"Yes. The power company's outage map showed power had been restored at midnight.\""), .cross("Did {D} turn the generator off when asked?", "\"Right away. {D} was apologetic and polite.\"")],
