        defendant: [.direct("Did you sign those checks?", "\"I filled them out. I signed them in a name I thought was mine to use, since I found the checkbook.\""), .direct("Whose name was on the checks?", "\"A name I got from a friend called Skip. I used what I was told to use.\""), .direct("Where did you find the checkbook?", "\"In a rental car I had driven. It was sitting in the car, and I picked it up.\""), .direct("Tell us how you came to have the checkbook.", "\"I found it in a rental car I had driven. It was in the glove box with a few papers.\""), .direct("What did you do with the checks?", "\"I filled out three, signed a name I got from a friend, and cashed them. I needed money and told myself I'd repay it.\""), .direct("What did you tell the teller?", "\"That the checks were from a friend. I wasn't trying to hide anything, and I used my own ID.\""), .cross("You cashed $480 in checks that did not belong to you, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I needed the money, and I did not think about whose it was.\""), .cross("Why use your real ID if you thought you were doing something wrong?", "\"Because I did not think I was. I thought the checks were fair to use.\""), .cross("You signed a name that wasn't yours. Isn't that forgery?", "\"It is, and I know it. I wasn't thinking about the law, I was thinking about money.\""), .cross("Your friend 'Skip' left the area. Can anyone confirm that?", "\"No. I don't have a way to reach Skip, and I wish I did.\""), .cross("The name on the checks did not match yours, did it?", "\"No. It did not. I thought the owner would never notice, and I know signing a name that is not mine was wrong.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} cashed three checks from a checkbook found in a rental car, signing a name that was not {D}'s, for a total of $480. The bank flagged all three two days later.", "The defense witnesses will explain that {D} found the checkbook in a car, did not hide behind a false ID, and did not understand that using the checks was wrong."),
